  "live_records": {
    "q-83946": {
      "dom_id": "step-q83946",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14129233/assets/31054ef4614814dd1c9131192504ea37f3527af75d8292fbce943c16235c9303.png)\n\nThe region $D$ in the second quadrant is enclosed between two quarter-circles centered at $O$ of radii $1$ and $3,$ as shown above. What is\n${∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A$ \nexpressed in polar coordinates?",
      "worked_solution": "We will use the change of variables formula in the form \n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}f(x,y)\\text{ }dA={∬}_{Δ}\\text{ }f(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\text{ }drd\\theta .\n$$\n\nThe region $D$ represents a portion of the washer enclosed between the circles of radii $1$ and $3$ centered at the origin. In polar coordinates $(r,\\theta ),$ the region can be expressed as \n\n$$\nΔ=\\{(r,\\theta )\\,:\\,1\\le r\\le 3,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\le \\theta \\le \\pi \\}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, using the change of variables formula, we obtain  \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}(x+y)\\,\\text{d}A & ={∬}_{Δ}(r\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +r\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta )\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}(r(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ))\\,r\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta  \\\\  & ={\\int }_{\\pi /2}^{\\pi }{\\int }_{1}^{3}{r}^{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta )\\,\\text{d}r\\,\\text{d}\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
